        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: expose AWS instance-profile state in inspect",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw cloud-worker admission must prove that a direct AWS lease has no IAM instance profile. Local configuration and guest-side metadata probes do not authoritatively describe the EC2 control-plane attachment state.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDirect AWS inspection now derives `providerMetadata.instanceProfileAttached` from the `DescribeInstances` response. `inspect --json` exposes only that documented boolean; unrelated or invalid provider metadata remains private and omitted.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSecurity-sensitive consumers can fail closed unless Crabbox authoritatively reports that an AWS lease has no instance profile attached.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `go test ./internal/cli` (green, 136.117s final exact run)\n- Focused attachment/status tests, including incomplete SDK metadata, false-value preservation, invalid metadata omission, and internal-field non-disclosure\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode uncommitted --base origin/main` (clean; no accepted/actionable findings)\n",
